.TH XDSH 1 "September 2026" "xcat-ports 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xdsh \- parallel distributed shell execution for cluster nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xdsh
\fInoderange\fR
[\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-ignore\-host\-key\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIfanout\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fItimeout\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-Q\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR]
[\fB\-\-nodestatus\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIshell\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIscript\fR]
[\fB\-\-sudo\fR]
[\fB\-L\fR]
[\fB\-B\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR]
\fIcommand\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xdsh
is a standalone port of xCAT's \fBxdsh\fR utility running in bypass mode
(without requiring the \fBxcatd\fR daemon or an xCAT database). It resolves
the target \fInoderange\fR locally and executes commands in parallel across all
matching nodes using OpenSSH \fBssh\fR(1) (or another remote shell).
.PP
Each line of stdout and stderr is prefixed with the corresponding node name:
.IP
.nf
\fInode\fR: \fIoutput\fR
.fi
.PP
By default, output is buffered per node (printing stdout first, then stderr)
and printed in batches sorted by node name. Real-time streaming mode can be
enabled with \fB\-s\fR.
.PP
Remote command return codes are accurately captured via an injected marker
line (\fB:DSH_TARGET_RC=N:\fR) which is stripped from visible output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-host\-key\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-hostkey\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR, \fB\-\-no\-host\-key\-check\fR
Disable SSH host key verification. When specified, OpenSSH is invoked with:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o StrictHostKeyChecking=no\fR (accept unknown host keys automatically)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\fR (ignore user known_hosts file)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o GlobalKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\fR (ignore system known_hosts file)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o LogLevel=ERROR\fR (suppress host key addition warnings on stderr)
.RE
.IP
This option also applies to remote script copy via \fBscp\fR(1) when \fB\-e\fR is used.
Can also be enabled globally via the \fBXDSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY\fR or \fBDSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY\fR
environment variables.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fanout\fR \fIfanout\fR
Maximum number of concurrent remote processes to spawn simultaneously.
Default is \fB64\fR (configurable via \fBDSH_FANOUT\fR).
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIuser\fR
Remote login user ID. Defaults to current user (or \fBDSH_TO_USERID\fR).
A \fIuser\fR@\fInoderange\fR prefix on the noderange argument is also supported.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR
Execution inactivity timeout in seconds (configurable via \fBDSH_TIMEOUT\fR).
Default is \fB5\fR seconds. Specify \fB0\fR to disable the timeout.
If no output is received from in-flight children within the timeout period,
active child processes are terminated with \fBSIGINT\fR.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-stream\fR
Stream stdout and stderr lines immediately as they arrive from each node rather
than buffering per node.
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-silent\fR
Silent mode. Suppress standard command output from the remote nodes.
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-exit\-status\fR
Append a summary line \fBRemote_command_rc = \fIN\fR indicating the exit status
of the remote command for each node.
.TP
\fB\-\-nodestatus\fR
Output a status line for each node: \fB\fInode\fR: Remote_command_successful\fR or
\fB\fInode\fR: Remote_command_failed, error_code=\fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-monitor\fR
Display progress messages as commands start and finish on each node.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-trace\fR
Print each command invocation before running it.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-node\-rsh\fR \fIshell\fR
Path to the remote shell binary. Defaults to \fBssh\fR found in \fBPATH\fR,
or \fB/usr/bin/ssh\fR (configurable via \fBDSH_NODE_RSH\fR or \fBDSH_REMOTE_CMD\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-node\-options\fR \fIoptions\fR
Additional options passed directly to the remote shell command (configurable via
\fBDSH_NODE_OPTS\fR or \fBDSH_REMOTE_OPTS\fR).
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-execute\fR \fIscript\fR
Copy the local script file to \fB/tmp\fR on each target node via \fBscp\fR(1)
and execute it remotely, removing the temporary file afterward.
.TP
\fB\-\-sudo\fR
Prepend \fBsudo\fR to the remote command execution.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-no\-locale\fR
Do not prepend local locale environment variables to the remote command.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-bypass\fR
Bypass mode (accepted for compatibility; this standalone port always runs in bypass mode).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display command usage and exit.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-show\-config\fR
Display configuration parameters and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-X\fR, \fB\-\-noexpand\fR
Do not expand the noderange argument (accepted for compatibility).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY, DSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY
When set to \fB1\fR, \fBtrue\fR, \fByes\fR, or \fBon\fR, enables \fB\-k\fR host key
ignoring by default.
.TP
.B DSH_FANOUT
Default fanout value (concurrency level). Defaults to \fB64\fR.
.TP
.B DSH_TIMEOUT
Default command timeout in seconds (defaults to \fB5\fR; \fB0\fR disables timeout).
.TP
.B DSH_TO_USERID
Default remote user ID if not specified via \fB\-l\fR.
.TP
.B DSH_NODE_RSH, DSH_REMOTE_CMD
Default remote shell executable.
.TP
.B DSH_NODE_OPTS, DSH_REMOTE_OPTS
Default options to pass to the remote shell.
.TP
.B DSH_PATH
Path string exported as \fBPATH\fR in the pre-command on remote nodes.
.SH NODERANGE SYNTAX
Full xCAT noderange syntax is supported:
.TP
.B node1,node2
Comma-separated hostnames. Output is deduplicated and sorted.
.TP
.B node[1-100], node[001-200]
Numeric bracket ranges, preserving leading zeros.
.TP
.B rack1-rack4, node1:node200
Hyphen or colon ranges between hostnames.
.TP
.B 10.40.170.[71-80]
IPv4 bracket ranges.
.TP
.B ,-node3, -(node2,node4)
Exclusions (always applied last).
.TP
.B group1@group2
Intersection operator.
.TP
.B ^/path/to/file
Read hosts from a file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is equal to the number of failed target nodes (0 if all targets succeeded).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run uptime on a range of compute nodes:
.IP
.B xdsh node[1-20] uptime
.PP
Ignore SSH host key verification on newly installed nodes:
.IP
.B xdsh -k 10.40.170.[71-80] uptime
.PP
Execute a command as another user with sudo and stream output:
.IP
.B xdsh admin@node[1-4] --sudo -s "systemctl restart myapp"
.PP
Copy and execute a local script across the cluster with fanout of 16:
.IP
.B xdsh node[1-128] -f 16 -e ./update_configs.sh
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pping (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR scp (1)
